@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title What the probes measured before the TUI upgrades — the stdin pump, a silent teardown, Ctrl+C after exit, and a Bubble Tea Program on the proxy
' purpose: the measurements that decided the TUI upgrades, kept after the plan that held them was retired
' status: measured 2026-11-10 at 0f34a714 on darwin/arm64, go1.26.5, tmux 3.7b; a record, not a contract.
'   Every file:line below names the tree at 0f34a714. Most of that code is gone.
'   what was built from C1 ............ _spec/internal/ptyproxy/pty-ownership.puml
'   what was built from C2 and C3 ..... _spec/internal/backend/teardown.puml
'   the stack the spikes chose ........ _spec/internal/choiceui/tui-stack.puml
'   the prompt segment ................ _spec/internal/results/result-store.puml
'   what init installs for it ......... _spec/internal/promptkit/prompt-kit.puml
'   the order it all landed in ........ _spec/_plans/tui-upgrades-delivery.puml
'   sbx's own TUI, observed ........... _spec/_experiments/sbx-tui-observed.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
' These sections were the measured half of the responsiveness plan. Its
' proposals shipped in W0 to W13 of the delivery plan and left with it; the
' measurements stay here, word for word.
'
' EVIDENCE, read 2026-11-10:
' https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/usage/
' https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/release-notes/
' https://pkg.go.dev/charm.land/bubbletea/v2
' https://github.com/charmbracelet/bubbletea/blob/main/UPGRADE_GUIDE_V2.md
' https://github.com/muesli/cancelreader
' https://github.com/muesli/cancelreader/blob/main/cancelreader_bsd.go
' https://github.com/golang/go/issues/24842
' https://pkg.go.dev/os/signal
' https://starship.rs/config/
' https://starship.rs/guide/
' https://github.com/starship/starship/releases/tag/v1.27.0
' https://github.com/ryanoasis/nerd-fonts/releases/tag/v3.5.1
' https://github.com/ryanoasis/nerd-fonts/blob/master/LICENSE
' https://github.com/LuisAlejandro/mash
' https://github.com/gdamore/tcell/releases
' Every measurement below ran on darwin/arm64, go1.26.5, tmux 3.7b.
' [Unverified] Nothing here was run on Linux.
'
'
' ── C1 · MEASURED: THE STDIN PUMP OUTLIVES Run AND TAKES THE NEXT KEYS ─────
' Proxy.Run starts `go p.pumpIn()` and returns without stopping it
' (ptyproxy.go:109). readChunks stays parked in read(0). After the pump itself
' returned it still takes 33 chunks: 32 buffered (ptyproxy.go:188) and one held
' in the blocked send (:195).
' pty-ownership.puml records the first half: "The IN pump cannot be waited on".
' It names tcell.NewScreen as the second-reader trap DURING a run.
' Teardown builds that second reader AFTER the run: confirm.go:25 openScreen
' calls tcell.NewScreen for the pushed-branch question (pushed.go:20-30).
' That is the ONLY terminal read after Run in the process: internal/run and
' cmd/proveo only print and exit.
'
' Throwaway probes ran through `go test -overlay`; the tree was not modified.
'   mechanism  A pty pair stood in for the operator terminal. Ten keys were
'              typed after Run returned, twenty rounds. A second reader
'              received 95 of 200 keys; a re-run gave 93. Every round lost at
'              least one. Control without Run: 200 of 200.
'   live       The real choiceui.ConfirmFetchPushed over tcell.NewScreen,
'              after a real Run, in tmux. The operator typed y, then Enter.
'              Twelve rounds: accepted 0, declined 10, still open after 4s 2.
'              A re-run gave accepted 1, declined 5, still open 6.
'              Control without Run: accepted 12 of 12.
' The split between "declined" and "still open" is not stable. The pin must
' require acceptance in EVERY round.
' So the first key after the agent exits goes to the dead pump. `y` vanishes.
' Enter arrives alone and reads as N, or the modal waits out its 15s timer.
' The same pump takes type-ahead meant for the shell while teardown runs.
' [Inference] This is the reported post-exit freeze. It matches the symptom and
' its timing. No operator session was recorded to confirm it.
'
' WHY GO CANNOT STOP THAT READ. os.Stdin is a blocking file. SetReadDeadline
' is refused on it, and Close does not unblock a read in progress
' (golang/go#24842, Ian Lance Taylor: "it won't unblock a `read`"). Flipping
' fd 0 to non-blocking changes the open file description the shell shares; the
' same issue calls that "both unusual and risky".
'
' THREE WAYS TO STOP IT, EACH PROTOTYPED (D1).
'   (a) muesli/cancelreader, the reader sbx 0.50.0 embeds (v0.2.2, MEASURED with
'       `go version -m`). Wrapped plainly around p.In it FAILS the repo's -race
'       gate, 3 of 3 runs: it calls file.Fd() on every wait. It also leaves
'       the reader alive when fd 0 is /dev/tty under the name /dev/stdin (Run
'       took 1.004s). With a two-method File adapter (a captured Fd, and
'       Name() = "/dev/tty") it passes everything (b) passes.
'   (b) select(2) plus a self-pipe through golang.org/x/sys/unix: 71 new lines,
'       no new module. The pinned test passed 20 of 20 rounds, the live modal
'       12 of 12, the package under -race 3 of 3. It joined in 3ms.
'   (c) keep the pump and route post-exit prompts through the hand-off channel.
'       It crosses 4 files in 2 packages, needs a new exported method mirrored
'       in the Windows stub, and cannot pass the pin "a second reader gets
'       every key".
' The 41-line change to Run and readChunks is the same for (a) and (b).
' A live Ctrl+C overlay must END with the child first: with the join alone, an
' overlay open at child exit never receives another key (MEASURED).
'
' ── C2 · TEARDOWN SAYS NOTHING WHILE IT WORKS ──────────────────────────────
' Teardown is one deferred closure (sandbox.go:1732-1817). On a clone run, the
' default, it starts up to 31 subprocesses: 7 `sbx ls`, 11 other sbx calls and
' 13 host git or tar calls. A direct-mount run starts about 11.
' A line prints when a step ENDS, with two exceptions (sandbox.go:1730, :1807).
' internal/ui has no live line.
' Ceilings, MEASURED by reading the calls:
'   34s   reportCredentialInUse: a 10s `sbx ls`, a 20s exec, 2s grace on each
'   36s   the clone-mode probe; it can run twice in one teardown
'   10s   policy log, memory evidence, each `sbx ls` behind Running / Exists
'   3m    EACH of: .env read, snapshot, lift, remote fetch, bundle, span, rebase
'   none  four guest or network calls: sandboxReflog, the pushed-branch
'         `git fetch`, SaveState and teardown's `sbx rm --force`
'   none  nine host-local git and tar calls
'   30s   stopWait after the Ctrl+C modal's y. The agent's screen is repainted
'         and nothing says a stop is in flight.
'   2s    drainGrace when a grandchild still holds the PTY slave
' THE FIRST UNBOUNDED CALL RUNS BEFORE THE CARRY. sbx.Exists answers true when
' `sbx ls` fails. On a wedged daemon a clone run waits 10s, then starts
' sandboxReflog with no deadline. Teardown stops there, prints nothing, and no
' work has reached home.
' [Unverified] Typical durations are unknown. The run log stamps section
' headers only, so no finished run yields per-step time. P0 adds that.
' THE OLLAMA PULL IS A DEFECT, NOT A PRECEDENT. It writes every frame through
' Default.W after the tee (host_ollama.go:242), so its frames reach the run
' log with their carriage returns (probe: 3 frames, 4 CRs). ui's wrapper also
' splits a wide frame and measures "\x1b[K" plus text as width 0. A live line
' needs a terminal-only writer under Printer.mu.
' kit-lifecycle.puml already decided "a 3m deadline plus a rescue recipe" for
' SaveState and `sbx rm`, and marks both STILL OPEN.
' sbx's own answer, v0.51.0 release notes: "Progress shows command
' descriptions", `--no-progress`, and "Canceled sandbox and environment
' creation exits with status 130 and a clear message".
'
' ── C3 · CTRL+C AFTER THE AGENT EXITS IS UNDEFINED ─────────────────────────
' forwardStop registers SIGTERM and SIGHUP only (sandbox.go:1834). Every
' SIGTERM and SIGHUP in teardown is swallowed, the first included: the parked
' goroutine consumes it and cancels only runCtx, and signalled() was already
' read at sandbox.go:1728.
' SIGINT has no handler. Run restores cooked mode before teardown, so Ctrl+C is
' a real SIGINT to the foreground process group. Go's default ends the process:
' "A SIGHUP, SIGINT, or SIGTERM signal causes the program to exit" (os/signal).
' Deferred functions do not run. That skips homeAccess.Commit and Cleanup,
' SaveState, `sbx rm`, KeptLines, the run log's close and recordOutcome.
' Nothing prints about what was left.
' MEASURED with a probe in tmux: a handler alone does not protect the work. A
' plain child died on the first Ctrl+C ("signal: interrupt"). A Setpgid child
' survived it. The second press cancelled a context whose Cancel signalled the
' group; the child died in 2ms and the shell read exit 130.
' Run returns an unnamed result and evaluates it before any defer runs, so the
' closure cannot make proveo exit 130. Teardown must become an explicit call.
' [Inference] A silent terminal invites Ctrl+C, so C2 feeds C3.
' sbx's dashboard, MEASURED 0.50.0 in tmux: the footer always shows "^c quit".
' The first Ctrl+C opens "Exit — Do you want to exit?" with No selected. Esc
' closes it. A second Ctrl+C quits with status 0. Sandboxes stay untouched.
'
' ── STARSHIP: WHAT IT IS, AND WHAT P4 SHIPS ────────────────────────────────
' mash does not use starship as a TUI library. MEASURED from its repository:
' packaging/assets.json pins starship v1.27.0, packaging/defaults/starship.toml
' seeds the prompt, and the bash and fish rc files run `starship init`. It is
' the SHELL PROMPT inside mash's bundled terminal.
' starship is a Rust binary the shell calls once per prompt. Its contract is a
' budget: scan_timeout 30 ms, command_timeout 500 ms.
'   THE BUDGET. Every teardown step gets a named ceiling and a visible clock.
'   THE LIFETIME ANSWER (D4). proveo exits. The shell prompt carries
'     "1 kept · 2 to adopt" from a state store through a `[custom.proveo]`
'     module.
' MEASURED with starship 1.27.0 against a scratch config:
'   `when` defaults to false: a module without `when = true` never shows
'   `require_repo = true` hides the module outside a git repository
'   a command that prints nothing still draws a styled space, unless the
'     format is `[($output )]($style)`
'   a command over the budget prints two [WARN] lines above the prompt
'   the module costs 11 ms; proveo itself starts in 20-27 ms; `sbx ls` takes
'     237-483 ms, so `proveo prompt` must never call sbx
' "Refs to adopt" cannot be derived at prompt time: 51 of 57 sessions here sit
' only in packed-refs, and 47 of 63 carried refs are already reachable from a
' branch. The count is computed with git at teardown and stored.
' The store lives under `<state>/results/`, one file per entry. `proveo clean`
' removes `<state>/runs/<sid>` by pid liveness while the sandbox still exists,
' and three live runs here share one git common dir, so one index file races.
' Carried refs also appear at run START (a retired sandbox), so PreserveClone
' records them, not the teardown closure.
' A record written only at the end of teardown is lost on the SIGINT kill of
' C3. The store needs a write-ahead entry.
' Verbs: `proveo adopt` and `proveo rm`. Neither overlaps an existing command.
' CloneRescueLines stays as the fallback recipe: it prints when the carry
' FAILED, and `proveo rm` retries that carry first.
'
'
' ── THE STACK, AND WHY IT IS NOT THE CAUSE ─────────────────────────────────
' proveo: tcell v2.6.0 (upstream v3.6.0, 2026-10-11), creack/pty,
' go-fuzzyfinder v0.9.0, and a hand-rolled ANSI stream.
' sbx 0.50.0: bubbletea/v2 2.0.10, lipgloss/v2 2.0.6, bubbles/v2 2.2.1,
' ultraviolet, cancelreader 0.2.2 (MEASURED).
' C1, C2 and C3 need no framework change. D3 ports anyway.
'
'
' ── THE PORT (D3): WHAT THE SPIKES MEASURED ────────────────────────────────
' THE GATE PASSES (P5a). Two independent lanes ran a Bubble Tea v2.1.1 Program
' on a copy of the proxy's hand-off reader in tmux. It opened no /dev/tty, saw
' 0 of 20 withheld keys, and Run returned under 1 ms after Quit with no
' further byte. The next key reached the session.
' THE GATE DOES NOT NEED P1. The overlay runs while Proxy.Run is alive.
' P1 GATES EVERYTHING AFTER Run. A default-input Program started after Run
' received 14 of 100 keys.
' WHAT THE PORT MUST DO THAT THIS PLAN DID NOT LIST:
'   newlines  With non-TTY input the renderer assumes NL maps to CR NL
'             (tea.go:1107). The proxy keeps the terminal raw, so a frame came
'             out as "one\ntwo\nthree". An adapter is required: overlaytty.go
'             is REWRITTEN, not deleted.
'   halt      Halt the hand-off reader when the dialog quits. Without it a
'             chunk typed after Run returns goes to a dead goroutine (5 of 5).
'   signals   The library's handler acts on the first signal only; a second
'             SIGINT killed the process. Pass tea.WithoutSignalHandler and
'             run proveo's own loop.
'   keys      Ctrl+C typed on a raw TTY arrives as tea.KeyPressMsg, and a child
'             in the same group survived two presses. tea.InterruptMsg comes
'             only from SIGINT. A Program on a hand-off reader, or with
'             WithInput(nil), changes no termios: the headless path still needs
'             the process-group work of C3.
'   modes     Overlay Views set AltScreen and DisableBracketedPasteMode. With
'             input on, the Program writes two DECRQM queries, a kitty
'             keyboard push and query, and modifyOtherKeys 2; tcell writes
'             none. OPTION B avoids them: WithInput(nil), proveo decodes the
'             hand-off with ultraviolet and calls Program.Send. It costs a
'             direct import of an untagged module. Decided inside P5a.
'   output    tcell draws on /dev/tty; a Program defaults to stdout. Every
'             ported surface passes the tty as output.
'   handover  ReleaseTerminal and tea.Exec on a hand-off reader stall 500 ms and
'             lose the first key (10 of 10). Use them only where the Program
'             reads the real stdin, and not inside the startup probe window.
'   headless  The library has no plain rendering: stdout to a file gave 844
'             bytes of control sequences. proveo keeps its own non-TTY branch.
'   Println   The doc says it prints nothing on the alt screen. The code has
'             no such guard (tea.go:892-893).
'   EnvMsg    Never log it. It carries the whole process environment.
' bubbles/v2 v2.2.1 has tree, textinput, viewport, spinner, stopwatch, timer,
' help, key, paginator and list. It has no form, radio, checkbox or button.
' lipgloss.HasDarkBackground and tea.RequestBackgroundColor read the terminal.
' No proveo view calls them: the proxy owns that reader.
' THE TMUX TEST DOES NOT STAY UNCHANGED. Its helper half builds the dialog
' through tcell (e2e/close_confirm_live_test.go:112-131). The driver half
' (:23-92) stays.
' bubbletea v2.1.1 and cancelreader v0.2.2 cross-build for all eight release
' targets with CGO_ENABLED=0 under go1.26.5.
'

component "C1 · the stdin pump\noutlives Run, takes the next keys" as C1 <<error>>
component "C2 · teardown\nup to 31 subprocesses, silent" as C2 <<error>>
component "C3 · Ctrl+C after exit\nno handler; deferred work is skipped" as C3 <<error>>
component "the spikes\na Bubble Tea Program on the hand-off reader" as SPIKE <<app>>
component "starship\na budget, and 11 ms for the module" as STAR <<cloud>>
component "what was built\nthe specs each wave wrote" as BUILT <<host>>

C1 ARROW_MAIN BUILT : pty-ownership
C2 ARROW_MAIN BUILT : teardown
C3 ARROW_MAIN BUILT : teardown
SPIKE ARROW_MAIN BUILT : tui-stack
STAR ARROW_OPTIONAL BUILT : result-store · prompt-kit

note bottom of C1
  **The first key went to a dead reader.** A
  second reader of the terminal got 95 of 200
  keys after Run returned, and the question
  accepted y then Enter 0 times in 12.
end note

note bottom of C2
  **A line printed when a step ended.** Seven
  steps could each wait three minutes, four
  calls had no deadline, and nothing drew
  while any of them ran.
end note

note bottom of C3
  **Ctrl+C ended proveo on the spot.** No
  handler existed, the terminal was back in
  cooked mode, and no deferred call ran: no
  carry, no state save, no removal.
end note

note bottom of SPIKE
  **The gate passed before the port began.** A
  Program on a copy of the hand-off reader
  opened no terminal of its own and took none
  of 20 withheld keys.
end note

note bottom of STAR
  **A prompt has a budget.** starship allows a
  command 500 ms. The module costs 11 ms and
  ""sbx ls"" up to 483, so the segment reads a
  stored count and never calls sbx.
end note
@enduml
